# Code-First OpenAPI Routes with Zod and Next.js

This rule establishes the pattern for creating type-safe, self-documenting API routes using `@omer-x/next-openapi-route-handler` with Zod schemas. The Zod schemas serve as both runtime validation and the source for OpenAPI documentation generation.

## Core Principles

1. **Single Source of Truth**: Zod schemas drive both validation and OpenAPI docs
2. **Type Safety**: TypeScript types are inferred from Zod schemas
3. **Runtime Validation**: All inputs validated automatically via Zod
4. **Auto Documentation**: OpenAPI spec generated from route definitions
5. **Bearer Auth**: All routes use `Authorization: Bearer <api_key>` authentication
6. **Preserve Logic**: Existing auth, logging, and business logic remain unchanged

## Dependencies

These packages are already installed:
- `@omer-x/next-openapi-route-handler` - Route wrapper with OpenAPI metadata
- `@omer-x/next-openapi-json-generator` - OpenAPI spec generator (for future use)
- `zod` - Schema validation library

## Error Response Standard (RFC 9457)

All API errors MUST follow the RFC 9457 Problem Details standard with enhancements for better developer experience.

### Error Schema Structure

```typescript
// app/api/v2/schemas/errors.ts
import { z } from "zod"

export const ErrorCategoryEnum = z.enum([
  'authentication_error',
  'authorization_error',
  'validation_error',
  'not_found_error',
  'conflict_error',
  'rate_limit_error',
  'server_error'
])

export const ErrorFieldSchema = z.object({
  field: z.string(),
  code: z.string(),
  message: z.string(),
})

export const ApiErrorSchema = z.object({
  // RFC 9457 standard fields
  type: z.string().url(),
  title: z.string(),
  status: z.number().int().min(100).max(599),
  detail: z.string(),
  instance: z.string(),
  
  // Enhanced fields for Inbound
  code: z.string(),
  category: ErrorCategoryEnum,
  field: z.string().optional(),
  errors: z.array(ErrorFieldSchema).optional(),
  request_id: z.string(),
  timestamp: z.string().datetime(),
  doc_url: z.string().url().optional(),
  suggestion: z.string().optional(),
})

export type ApiError = z.infer<typeof ApiErrorSchema>
```

### Error Builder Helper

```typescript
// app/api/v2/schemas/errors.ts
export function buildApiError(params: {
  status: number
  code: string
  title: string
  detail: string
  instance: string
  category: z.infer<typeof ErrorCategoryEnum>
  field?: string
  errors?: Array<{ field: string; code: string; message: string }>
  suggestion?: string
  requestId: string
}): ApiError {
  return {
    type: `https://api.inbound.new/errors/${params.code.toLowerCase().replace(/_/g, '-')}`,
    title: params.title,
    status: params.status,
    detail: params.detail,
    instance: params.instance,
    code: params.code,
    category: params.category,
    field: params.field,
    errors: params.errors,
    request_id: params.requestId,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    doc_url: `https://docs.inbound.new/errors/${params.code.toLowerCase().replace(/_/g, '-')}`,
    suggestion: params.suggestion,
  }
}
```

